    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full suite is green (39/39 passing, BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## What I did\n\nConsolidated the three separate duplicate checks (telephone, email, household) into a single derived `identityKey = normalizedTelephone + '|' + (email or empty) + '|' + householdId`, rejecting with **409** only on a whole-key match.\n\n**New pieces**\n- `OwnerIdentity` \u2014 a helper with `identityKey(telephone, email, householdId)`: telephone normalized to E.164 (idempotent, matching the stored form), email lower-cased, each of email/householdId empty when absent.\n- `RequireUniqueOwnerIdentity` \u2014 the single duplicate step: builds the new owner's key and rejects only when it exactly equals an existing owner's key.\n- `OwnerIdentityDuplicateException` (checked) + handler responding `409 {\"errors\":[\"identityKey\"]}` + its escalation YAML.\n\n**Wiring & response**\n- `owners.POST.yml`: removed the `uniqueEmail`/`unique`/`household` steps; inserted the new `identity` step **after** `assignHousehold` so the `householdId` segment is populated (and household members get back-filled) before the key is compared.\n- Added a read-only `identityKey` to the `Owner` schema in `openapi.yml` and a MapStruct expression mapping so `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it.\n\n**Behaviour change verified by the tests**\n- Exact full-key duplicates still 409 (Cp03, Cp25, Cp28), and same-household + same-telephone still 409 (Cp10).\n- Because telephone is part of the key, two members of the same household with **different** telephones now both succeed and share a `householdId` while having distinct `identityKey`s (Cp11).\n\nThe former telephone/email/household check classes and their exceptions/handlers are left in place only as inert dead code \u2014 two of them still provide static helpers (`NormalizeOwnerTelephone.toE164`, `RequireUniqueOwnerHousehold.normalize`) that other active steps depend on. I left them rather than risk breaking those dependencies or a `@link` in a javadoc; say the word if you'd like me to fully prune the unused ones.",
